And he's like, Angela, I need to roll an eight.
然后他说：“安吉拉，我需要摇出一个八点。”

918
00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:48.700
And everyone wins.
“然后大家就都赢了。”

919
00:41:48.800 --> 00:41:50.340
And she says, So roll an eight.
她说：“那就摇出一个八点呗。”

920
00:41:50.700 --> 00:41:52.160
And then he does.
然后他就摇出来了。

921
00:41:52.440 --> 00:41:52.860
Yes!
太棒了！

922
00:41:53.280 --> 00:41:58.640
And he is so excited that he grabs you and he kisses you on the cheek.
他激动得抓住了你，还在你脸颊上亲了一下。

923
00:41:58.940 --> 00:41:59.820
I know.
我知道。

924
00:41:59.820 --> 00:42:02.760
And listen, even though maybe she's happy about that,
听着，尽管她可能为此感到高兴，

925
00:42:02.940 --> 00:42:06.180
she has to slap him for being inappropriate at work.
但她还是得扇他一巴掌，因为他在工作场合举止不当。

926
00:42:06.380 --> 00:42:06.820
Yes.
没错。

927
00:42:07.440 --> 00:42:10.840
Well, Angela, we got a fan question from Heather Lindo.
好吧，安吉拉，我们收到了来自海瑟·琳多的粉丝提问。

928
00:42:11.300 --> 00:42:12.480
Sam, will you play it?
萨姆，能放一下吗？

929
00:42:12.480 --> 00:42:13.180
Hi, Jenna.
嗨，珍娜。

930
00:42:13.400 --> 00:42:13.920
Hi, Angela.
嗨，安吉拉。

931
00:42:14.620 --> 00:42:18.480
Casino Night is one of my very favorite episodes for a lot of reasons.
《赌场之夜》是我最喜欢的剧集之一，原因有很多。

932
00:42:18.480 --> 00:42:24.600
And one of them being the scene at the craps table when Dwight kisses Angela for good luck
其中之一就是双骰赌桌旁的那场戏，德怀特为了好运气亲吻了安吉拉，

933
00:42:24.600 --> 00:42:25.740
and then she slaps him.
然后她扇了他一巴掌。

934
00:42:26.000 --> 00:42:29.500
But when she turns around, her face is just perfection.
但当她转过身时，她的表情简直完美。

935
00:42:29.800 --> 00:42:33.000
She cycles through like 10 emotions in a matter of like three seconds.
她在大概三秒钟内经历了大约10种情绪。

936
00:42:33.000 --> 00:42:39.520
She is horrified and thrilled and embarrassed and obviously deep down very happy all at the same time.
她感到惊恐、兴奋、尴尬，显然内心深处又非常高兴，这一切同时发生。

937
00:42:39.900 --> 00:42:41.060
And I just love it.
我太喜欢了。

938
00:42:41.060 --> 00:42:47.060
And Angela, my question is, did you nail that on the first take or did you have to do it many, many times?
安吉拉，我的问题是，你是一条过，还是拍了很多很多遍？

939
00:42:47.280 --> 00:42:49.860
Thank you so much for letting me ask my question.
非常感谢让我有机会提问。

940
00:42:50.000 --> 00:42:54.660
I know everyone says this, but my sister Kim and I really are the Office number one fans.
我知道每个人都这么说，但我和我妹妹金真的是《办公室》的头号粉丝。

941
00:42:54.760 --> 00:42:55.660
We just love you so much.
我们太喜欢你们了。

942
00:42:55.740 --> 00:42:56.220
So thank you.
所以谢谢你们。

943
00:42:56.500 --> 00:42:59.140
So sweet.
太贴心了。

944
00:42:59.140 --> 00:43:00.760
I love that question so much.
我太喜欢这个提问了。

945
00:43:01.620 --> 00:43:02.020
Okay.
好的。

946
00:43:02.020 --> 00:43:08.240
So I was very excited about this question because I actually wrote in my journal about the scene.
我对这个问题非常兴奋，因为我确实在日记里写过这场戏。

947
00:43:08.620 --> 00:43:09.560
Of course you did.
你当然写了。

948
00:43:09.760 --> 00:43:10.400
Of course we did.
我们当然都写了。

949
00:43:10.520 --> 00:43:12.020
I wrote about it the week we filmed it.
我在我们拍摄的那周写了关于它的内容。

950
00:43:12.220 --> 00:43:17.500
To answer your question, Heather, no, I did not get it right the first time.
回答你的问题，海瑟，没有，我不是一次就拍成功的。

951
00:43:17.820 --> 00:43:18.160
Okay.
好的。

952
00:43:18.240 --> 00:43:21.540
So I wrote that I was really nervous to slap Rain at firSt.
所以我写道，我一开始扇雷恩耳光的时候真的很紧张。

953
00:43:21.660 --> 00:43:23.280
You know, my slap was kind of timid.
你知道的，我的耳光有点畏缩。

954
00:43:23.280 --> 00:43:27.140
Which makes sense because you were probably very, you were worried about hurting him.
这很合理，因为你可能很，你担心弄疼他。

955
00:43:27.640 --> 00:43:28.080
Exactly.
没错。

956
00:43:28.080 --> 00:43:29.160
I didn't want to hurt him.
我不想弄疼他。

957
00:43:29.300 --> 00:43:30.580
And it wasn't a fake slap.
而且这不是假打。

958
00:43:30.820 --> 00:43:32.200
They told you to really slap him.
他们让你真打他。

959
00:43:32.300 --> 00:43:34.280
That was, they were never did a phony slap.
那是，他们从来不做假耳光。

960
00:43:34.480 --> 00:43:36.000
No, they wanted a real slap.
不，他们想要一个真实的耳光。

961
00:43:36.220 --> 00:43:39.260
And well, I guess my timid little slap wasn't working.
然后，我想我那胆小的小耳光没起作用。

962
00:43:39.820 --> 00:43:42.880
So Rain said, listen, Ange, just go for it.
所以雷恩说，听着，安吉，放手去打吧。

963
00:43:43.020 --> 00:43:44.020
I can take it.
我能承受。

964
00:43:44.240 --> 00:43:47.480
So I started really slapping him.
所以我开始狠狠地扇他耳光。

965
00:43:47.560 --> 00:43:48.240
Oh, no.
噢，不。

966
00:43:48.520 --> 00:43:52.340
And I wrote that it took us about 13 takes to get.
我写道，我们大概拍了13条才完成。

967
00:43:52.380 --> 00:43:52.860
Oh, no.
噢，不。

968
00:43:53.040 --> 00:43:53.420
Yes.
是的。

969
00:43:53.980 --> 00:43:56.600
So that's 13 slaps.
所以那是13个耳光。

970
00:43:56.940 --> 00:43:57.300
All right.
好吧。

971
00:43:57.500 --> 00:43:59.320
Here's the one thing I need you guys to remember.
有一件事我需要你们记住。

972
00:43:59.560 --> 00:44:00.980
I am 5'1".
我身高五尺一寸。

973
00:44:00.980 --> 00:44:02.520
Rain is like 6'3".
雷恩身高大概六尺三寸。

974
00:44:02.520 --> 00:44:06.100
So it wasn't really easy for me to reach his cheek.
所以我要够到他的脸并不容易。

975
00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:09.100
And one time my aim was really off.
有一次我的准头真的偏了。

976
00:44:09.260 --> 00:44:10.420
And I missed his cheek.
我没打中他的脸。

977
00:44:10.480 --> 00:44:13.540
And I slapped his ear so hard.
我狠狠地扇了他的耳朵一下。

978
00:44:13.880 --> 00:44:15.980
He was like, I'd actually hurt him.
他当时的样子，我真的弄疼他了。

979
00:44:16.080 --> 00:44:17.580
You said there was like a ringing in his ear.
你说过他的耳朵里好像有耳鸣声。

980
00:44:17.780 --> 00:44:19.440
And then the other time I missed.
还有一次我打偏了。

981
00:44:19.620 --> 00:44:22.040
And I slapped and I hit his glasses.
我一巴掌打到了他的眼镜上。

982
00:44:22.040 --> 00:44:24.600
And I knocked them sideways on his face.
把他的眼镜打得在脸上歪向了一边。

983
00:44:24.840 --> 00:44:25.380
I know.
我知道。

984
00:44:25.920 --> 00:44:26.700
I know.
我知道。

985
00:44:27.780 --> 00:44:30.820
Well, I want to go back to something that Heather said, too,
嗯，我想回到海瑟刚才说过的一点上，

986
00:44:30.940 --> 00:44:34.080
about that look on your face as you're walking away.
关于你走开时脸上的那种表情。

987
00:44:34.200 --> 00:44:34.400
Yeah.
是啊。

988
00:44:34.540 --> 00:44:36.820
Because it is, it is amazing.
因为那个表情真的，真的太绝了。

989
00:44:37.440 --> 00:44:40.120
And I have the script and I looked it up.
我有剧本，我查了一下。

990
00:44:40.200 --> 00:44:46.820
And all it says is that you slapped Dwight and that you smile as you walk away from the table.
上面只写着你扇了德怀特耳光，并且你从桌子旁走开时微笑了。

991
00:44:47.080 --> 00:44:50.120
I think there's so much more going on in your face.
我觉得你脸上的戏远不止这些。

992
00:44:50.120 --> 00:44:55.080
So your character is angry that Dwight would kiss you so publicly and all of that.
所以你的角色很生气，因为德怀特竟然当众吻你之类的事情。

993
00:44:55.220 --> 00:45:00.620
But what I love is that you have this little look to the camera at the very end.
但最让我喜欢的是，你在最后对镜头有这样一个微小的眼神交流。

994
00:45:00.620 --> 00:45:03.180
It's like 18 minutes, 48 seconds.
大约在18分48秒的时候。

995
00:45:03.520 --> 00:45:04.040
Yeah.
对。

996
00:45:04.260 --> 00:45:08.760
Where you sort of catch the camera catching you smiling.
就是你好像发现了镜头拍到你在笑。

997
00:45:09.080 --> 00:45:09.180
Right.
没错。

998
00:45:09.240 --> 00:45:10.800
That camera catch was not in the script.
那个对镜头的捕捉并不在剧本里。

999
00:45:10.800 --> 00:45:11.880
Was that improvised?
那是即兴发挥的吗？

1000
00:45:12.160 --> 00:45:13.340
Yes, it was.
是的，是即兴的。

1001
00:45:13.560 --> 00:45:13.740
Okay.
好吧。

1002
00:45:13.840 --> 00:45:18.420
So that, that just happened on the day, that little moment where I'm busted at the end.
所以那件事就发生在当天，最后那个我被抓包的小瞬间。

1003
00:45:18.420 --> 00:45:24.840
And so in one of the early takes, I was walking out of frame and I just looked at camera and I
所以在其中一个早期镜头里，我正走出画幅，然后我只是看了一眼镜头，我

1004
00:45:24.840 --> 00:45:25.640
quickly looked away.
迅速移开了视线。

1005
00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:27.460
Like I was embarrassed that they caught me smiling.
就像我很不好意思被他们看到我在笑一样。

1006
00:45:27.680 --> 00:45:30.460
And our director of photography, Randall Einhorn said,
我们的摄影指导兰德尔·艾恩霍恩说，

1007
00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:31.720
Ange, Ange, I caught it.
安吉，安吉，我拍到了。

1008
00:45:31.800 --> 00:45:33.820
I caught it right at the end as you're leaving frame.
就在你离开画幅的最后关头，我拍到了。

1009
00:45:33.820 --> 00:45:36.500
And he really helped me find that moment.
他真的帮我找到了那个时刻。

1010
00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:38.240
Then he showed it to our director.
然后他把它放给我们的导演看。

1011
00:45:38.440 --> 00:45:39.420
Our director loved it.
我们的导演很喜欢。

1012
00:45:39.700 --> 00:45:44.260
And so Randall was like, Ange, you don't have a lot of time to cycle through all that,
所以兰德尔就说，安吉，你没有太多时间去经历所有这些情绪，

1013
00:45:44.360 --> 00:45:48.740
but I'm going to catch it every time if you glance to camera and quickly look away embarrassed.
但只要你瞟一眼镜头然后又害羞地迅速移开，我每次都能抓拍到。

1014
00:45:49.160 --> 00:45:53.000
So I have to thank Randall for that because he really helped me make that moment happen.
所以我得感谢兰德尔，因为他真的帮我促成了那一刻。

1015
00:45:53.240 --> 00:45:54.280
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

1016
00:45:54.480 --> 00:45:54.960
Yes.
是的。

1017
00:45:55.280 --> 00:45:58.340
All right, folks out there that love background catches.
好了，各位喜欢背景抓拍的朋友们。

1018
00:45:58.340 --> 00:46:03.900
I have one more moment for you in this little scene at 18 minutes, 51 seconds.
在这个小片段里，在18分51秒，我还有一个精彩瞬间要分享给你们。

1019
00:46:03.980 --> 00:46:09.120
You can really see how red the side of Rain's face is.
你们真的能看到雷恩的半边脸有多红。

1020
00:46:09.400 --> 00:46:12.760
And it's because I have slapped him 13 times.
那是因为我已经扇了他13个耳光了。

1021
00:46:14.260 --> 00:46:16.160
Well, there you have it.
好吧，事情就是这样。

1022
00:46:16.480 --> 00:46:18.300
Heather, thank you for such a great question.
海瑟，谢谢你提出这么棒的问题。

1023
00:46:18.620 --> 00:46:19.320
Thank you, Heather.
谢谢你，海瑟。

1024
00:46:19.540 --> 00:46:20.540
I love that question.
我很喜欢这个问题。

1025
00:46:20.920 --> 00:46:21.320
Okay.
好的。

1026
00:46:21.500 --> 00:46:28.260
So Angela, you just described the big kind of Dwight Angela flirt moment that happens in
那么安吉拉，你刚刚描述了德怀特和安吉拉之间那种盛大的调情时刻，就发生在

1027
00:46:28.260 --> 00:46:31.160
front of everybody at the casino night.
赌场之夜所有人的面前。

1028
00:46:31.360 --> 00:46:36.040
So now we head over to the poker table where it is heads up between Jim and Pam.
所以现在我们来到扑克桌旁，这里是吉姆和帕姆的单挑局。

1029
00:46:36.240 --> 00:46:41.320
And I feel like this is the big Jim-Pam flirt moment that's public.
我觉得这是吉姆和帕姆公开的重大调情时刻。

1030
00:46:41.560 --> 00:46:43.780
There is so much flirting happening.
这里有太多的调情发生了。

1031
00:46:44.140 --> 00:46:48.680
Pam is basically doing the giggle hair toss move from about last night.
帕姆基本上在用昨晚那种娇笑拨弄头发的招式。

1032
00:46:49.120 --> 00:46:51.360
I mean, it is on.
我的意思是，动真格的了。

1033
00:46:51.520 --> 00:46:52.100
It is on.
动真格的了。

1034
00:46:52.100 --> 00:46:55.100
Well, we had a fan question from Live Love California.
嗯，我们收到了来自“热爱加州”粉丝的提问。

1035
00:46:55.100 --> 00:46:59.880
The scene at the poker table when you and John are making those faces back and forth,
扑克桌旁的那场戏，当你和约翰眉来眼去地做那些表情时，

1036
00:47:00.140 --> 00:47:02.700
was that improvised or scripted?
那是即兴发挥的还是剧本写的？

1037
00:47:03.020 --> 00:47:04.560
This is what was scripted.
剧本里是这样写的。

1038
00:47:04.720 --> 00:47:05.900
Those little looks between us.
我们之间那些小眼神。

1039
00:47:06.020 --> 00:47:07.220
There was a scene description.
那里有一段场景描述。

1040
00:47:07.220 --> 00:47:10.020
And so what you're seeing is John and I's interpretation.
所以你们看到的是我和约翰的演绎。

1041
00:47:10.700 --> 00:47:14.300
This is what it says right after Jim's line, you're bluffing.
紧接着吉姆的台词“你在虚张声势”后面是这么写的：

1042
00:47:14.600 --> 00:47:17.860
Pam makes a playful gesture like, who knows?
帕姆做出一个调皮的手势，仿佛在说：谁知道呢？

1043
00:47:18.320 --> 00:47:20.120
Jim stares at her intensely.
吉姆专注地盯着她。

1044
00:47:20.880 --> 00:47:23.780
She smiles her best enigmatic smile.
她露出了她标志性的神秘微笑。

1045
00:47:24.160 --> 00:47:29.820
Jim enjoys this woman so much, he finally has to break eye contact and shake it off.
吉姆太喜欢这个女人了，他最终不得不移开视线并甩甩头来缓解。

1046
00:47:30.120 --> 00:47:30.500
Aww.
噢。

1047
00:47:31.480 --> 00:47:35.720
So that was what John and I, we had to take that note in the script.
所以这就是我和约翰当时必须领会的剧本提示。

1048
00:47:35.920 --> 00:47:38.360
And that's what made that scene.
这也是成就那场戏的原因。

1049
00:47:38.540 --> 00:47:39.820
Oh, that's so good.
哦，太棒了。

1050
00:47:39.820 --> 00:47:41.200
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

1051
00:47:41.600 --> 00:47:42.020
Yeah.
是啊。

1052
00:47:42.280 --> 00:47:43.540
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

1053
00:47:43.540 --> 00:47:49.080
Well, I have a question that's not related to you guys flirting, but at 19 minutes, 26
嗯，我有个问题跟你们俩打情骂俏无关，但在19分26

1054
00:47:49.080 --> 00:47:50.580
seconds, what the heck?
秒时，到底是怎么回事？

1055
00:47:50.740 --> 00:47:55.060
So Kevin wears glasses when he plays poker, but he doesn't wear glasses to be an accountant?
为什么凯文打扑克时戴眼镜，当会计时却不戴眼镜？

1056
00:47:55.700 --> 00:47:59.540
Angela, we literally got a fan question that said the same thing.
安吉拉，我们收到的粉丝提问里真的有说这个的。

1057
00:47:59.740 --> 00:48:00.580
What's up?
怎么回事？

1058
00:48:01.060 --> 00:48:04.900
My theory about that is that he doesn't care about being an accountant.
我对此的理论是，他根本不在乎当会计这事。

1059
00:48:04.980 --> 00:48:05.400
I know.
我知道。

1060
00:48:06.340 --> 00:48:12.700
But as he tells us, he has won one of the satellite games in the World Series of Poker.
但正如他所说，他赢过世界扑克系列赛的一场卫星赛。

1061
00:48:12.800 --> 00:48:14.640
He's an avid poker player, this guy.
这家伙可是个狂热的扑克玩家。

1062
00:48:15.020 --> 00:48:17.240
He's a different person when he's playing poker.
他打扑克的时候完全是另一个人。

1063
00:48:17.460 --> 00:48:20.440
He's a smart person when he's playing poker.
他打扑克的时候可聪明了。

1064
00:48:21.040 --> 00:48:24.000
But also when he's playing in his band, he wears a hat.
而且他去乐队演出时也会戴帽子。

1065
00:48:24.240 --> 00:48:24.760
I know.
我知道。

1066
00:48:24.920 --> 00:48:26.520
Like when he comes to the barbecue, he's got a hat.
就像他来烧烤派对时，也戴着帽子。

1067
00:48:26.620 --> 00:48:31.680
He's got a whole persona outside of the office that is very different than what we see on
他在办公室外有着完全不同的人设，跟我们平时

1068
00:48:31.680 --> 00:48:32.360
a daily basis.
看到的完全不一样。

1069
00:48:32.640 --> 00:48:33.240
Oh, for sure.
哦，确实。

1070
00:48:33.420 --> 00:48:33.980
For sure.
确实。

1071
00:48:33.980 --> 00:48:36.160
I want to follow this guy around.
真想跟着这家伙拍一天。

1072
00:48:36.340 --> 00:48:40.880
I feel, is he, is he putting us all on so that he doesn't really have to do work?
